def xml_children_as_dict(node):
    """Turn the children of node <xml> into a dict, keyed by tag name.

    This is only a shallow conversation - child nodes are not recursively processed.
    """
    children_dict = {}
    for child in node:
        if child.tag in children_dict:
            if not isinstance(children_dict[child.tag], list):
                children_dict[child.tag] = [children_dict[child.tag]]
            children_dict[child.tag].append(child.text)
        else:
            children_dict[child.tag] = child.text
    return children_dict
```

This function iterates over the children of the given XML node and constructs a dictionary where each key is a tag name and the value is the text content of the child node. If multiple children have the same tag, their text contents are stored in a list.

